  "description": "Five Monte Carlo dispersions no other template draws, in 12 runs: template 07's 150 kg microsatellite on wheels in Sun-safe pointing at 350 km. Each run draws any initial attitude, its body rate, its inertia, its SRP coefficient and the atmosphere's density scale. The spreads are illustrative.\n\nWhat to look at:\n- Run it in Monte Carlo mode (the mode beside Run): about half a minute in one process.\n- Runs: each run's draws: the attitude as MRP, the rates (nominal plus 0.2 deg/s 1-sigma), the inertia (1 kg m^2 1-sigma, turned by 2 deg), the SRP coefficient and the density scale.\n- Sensitivity: the density scale alone moves the orbit (rank correlation -1 with the lowest altitude).\n- The attitude, rate and inertia do not reach the orbit: with 12 runs, chance gives correlations up to 0.6.\n- Run This Case on any run: the wheels turn +z to the Sun within 5 minutes, from up to 132 deg away.\n\nTry changing:\n- The density scale's bounds (0.7 to 1.3), or a normal draw.\n- The body rate's 1-sigma to 2 deg/s: the wheels take longer.\n- More runs: the chance correlations become smaller.\n- After Save As: Scenario > Assumptions, New..., and set monte_carlo.spread_statistic to sample: the Statistics' standard deviations then divide by n - 1.\n\nNote:\n- The batch seed (44) gives the same draws every time, with one process or many.",
